& [Delineation]
  + provider protocol is deterministic construction and validation of public JSON records
  + provider execution is an HTTP or process effect and remains outside this slice
  + a provider response proves only conformance to the admitted envelope not correct reasoning authentic origin or external truth
  + one provider call corresponds to one separately verified compact advancement and never to an entire hidden multi-step drive

& [SelectedForms]
  + iterative_advance_request reconstructs the exact first or READY-continuation request from model prompt policy opening identity and verified prefix
  + admit_iterative_provider_iteration joins one sanitized conforming tool-call response to one separately verified single-advance deterministic result
  + validate_iterative_provider_prefix reconstructs every request parses every response and checks unique call identity quota predecessor sequence compact response and successor continuity
  + iterative_terminal_reflection_request reconstructs the full ordered public transcript and disables tools only after a terminal final iteration
  + no new provider transport process client or file-backed report is included

& [FacultyReview]
  + Honesty requires sanitized public response evidence and forbids attributing deterministic stepper output to the provider
  + Security requires host-selected quota custody closed call arguments unique call IDs and exact opening predecessor sequence
  + Planner requires call-count headroom before constructing another advance request and terminal-only reflection
  + Weaver requires deterministic message order assistant call then matching tool projection across the whole prefix
  + Scribe requires exact reconstructed requests sanitized responses compact responses and projections
  + Refiner requires projection-only tool messages with no context checkpoint body exact registry or private reasoning
  + Observer admits a record only when the provider half and deterministic half independently validate and their identities join

& [Decision]
  + activate an isolated pure provider_protocol Rust module and focused tests
  + permit no-network fixtures that synthesize response envelopes and use Slice2 in-memory single-advance results
  + retain Slice4 process orchestration provider execution report persistence remote access and effects under separate locks

& [Rollback]
  + new module exports and tests are additive and can be removed without changing P0 Slice1 or Slice2 data or behavior
